---
/**
 * Two itemised bills for two very different questions, side by side, with
 * identical totals.
 *
 * The teaching is done by the reader's own failed search for a difference. Both
 * panels list the same three junctions, the same three counts and the same
 * total; the ONLY thing that differs between them is the question printed at the
 * top. A caption that merely asserted "the work is fixed" would be read and
 * forgotten — a bill the reader compares line by line and finds identical is
 * harder to argue with.
 *
 * Every distinction here is typographic: headings, labels, digits and an equals
 * sign. Strip the colour out entirely and nothing is lost, because nothing was
 * ever carried by it (hard rule 9).
 *
 * The numbers are real for the network described in the unit — 784 inputs into
 * 512, into 512, into 10 — so a reader who multiplies them out gets the same
 * 668,672. Nothing here is rounded or invented.
 *
 * Decorative by itself, so `aria-hidden`: `Figure` supplies the accessible name
 * and the description.
 */
---

<svg viewBox="0 0 640 324" class="w-full" aria-hidden="true">
  <g class="fill-paper-sunken stroke-rule-strong" stroke-width="1.25">
    <rect x="8" y="16" width="288" height="248" rx="8"></rect>
    <rect x="344" y="16" width="288" height="248" rx="8"></rect>
  </g>

  <!-- The one thing that differs between the two panels. -->
  <g class="fill-ink-faint font-mono" font-size="8">
    <text x="26" y="40">THE QUESTION</text>
    <text x="362" y="40">THE QUESTION</text>
  </g>

  <g class="fill-ink font-display" font-size="13" font-weight="700">
    <text x="26" y="62">A 7 that anyone</text>
    <text x="26" y="79">reads at a glance</text>
    <text x="362" y="62">A 5 that three people</text>
    <text x="362" y="79">read differently</text>
  </g>

  <g class="stroke-rule" stroke-width="1">
    <line x1="26" y1="94" x2="278" y2="94"></line>
    <line x1="362" y1="94" x2="614" y2="94"></line>
  </g>

  <g class="fill-ink-faint font-mono" font-size="8">
    <text x="26" y="112">MULTIPLICATIONS, BY JUNCTION</text>
    <text x="362" y="112">MULTIPLICATIONS, BY JUNCTION</text>
  </g>

  <!-- Left panel: the itemised work. -->
  <g class="fill-ink-muted" font-size="11">
    <text x="26" y="134">784 pixels → 512 neurons</text>
    <text x="26" y="156">512 neurons → 512 neurons</text>
    <text x="26" y="178">512 neurons → 10 answers</text>
  </g>
  <g class="fill-ink font-mono" font-size="11" text-anchor="end">
    <text x="278" y="134">401,408</text>
    <text x="278" y="156">262,144</text>
    <text x="278" y="178">5,120</text>
  </g>

  <!-- Right panel: the same three lines, to the digit. -->
  <g class="fill-ink-muted" font-size="11">
    <text x="362" y="134">784 pixels → 512 neurons</text>
    <text x="362" y="156">512 neurons → 512 neurons</text>
    <text x="362" y="178">512 neurons → 10 answers</text>
  </g>
  <g class="fill-ink font-mono" font-size="11" text-anchor="end">
    <text x="614" y="134">401,408</text>
    <text x="614" y="156">262,144</text>
    <text x="614" y="178">5,120</text>
  </g>

  <g class="stroke-rule-strong" stroke-width="1.25">
    <line x1="26" y1="196" x2="278" y2="196"></line>
    <line x1="362" y1="196" x2="614" y2="196"></line>
  </g>

  <g class="fill-ink-faint font-mono" font-size="8">
    <text x="26" y="220">TOTAL FOR ONE SWEEP</text>
    <text x="362" y="220">TOTAL FOR ONE SWEEP</text>
  </g>

  <g
    class="fill-ink font-display"
    font-size="22"
    font-weight="700"
    text-anchor="end"
  >
    <text x="278" y="246">668,672</text>
    <text x="614" y="246">668,672</text>
  </g>

  <!-- The whole argument, in one glyph. -->
  <text
    x="320"
    y="152"
    class="fill-ink font-display"
    font-size="30"
    font-weight="700"
    text-anchor="middle">=</text
  >

  <text
    x="320"
    y="292"
    class="fill-ink font-display"
    font-size="12.5"
    font-weight="700"
    text-anchor="middle">Not similar. Identical, down to the last digit.</text
  >

  <text
    x="320"
    y="312"
    class="fill-ink-muted"
    font-size="10.5"
    text-anchor="middle"
    >Nothing about the question appears anywhere in the bill — the count is set
    by the wiring, and the wiring was fixed long before anyone asked.</text
  >
</svg>
